Package: DietView
Title: Interactive, Taxonomically Complete Visualization of Predator
    Diet from Stomach-Content Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sosthene", "A. V. Akia", email = "akiasosthene@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("CADI Gulf Center", role = c("aut", "cph")))
Description: Turns a long table of stomach-content records into interactive,
    taxonomically complete sunburst views of predator diet. Prey are resolved
    to the World Register of Marine Species ('WoRMS') classification, or joined
    from a user-supplied lineage table. Per-taxon relative importance is
    computed in occurrence and weight within each taxonomic rank, keeping
    unidentified prey as an explicit 'NA' category, and the identification bias
    associated with digestion level is quantified. Diet is rendered across any
    user-declared covariates (period, year, size class, length bins, region) as
    a 'shiny' application, a self-contained HTML dashboard, or 'plotly' figures,
    so that any survey formatted to a common input specification is
    reproducible.
